`the composed worker prompt is 33726 B, over the recorded bound of 29000 B` is the failure this change is about: the
file is byte-identical for every item and is re-sent with every turn, and 33 726 B is what the case's own throwaway
project renders from the base's template. It is also the figure `evidence/measure.log` measures for the same fixture
before the move.

Both runs were made on the restored base — `git reset --hard HEAD` — and the second one's `loop.conf` edit was undone
before the fix was applied, so the green of `evidence/green.log` is the same case over the fixed source and nothing
else.
